s reliability not explicit but decision quality suggests reliability. Also attention skills for C are excellent. So C may be overall stronger.\n\nThus I might shift my vote to Candidate C. Need to reference prior discussion: Agent 2 just argued for C, citing crew cooperation and stress resilience. I can either agree and also shift, or I could argue that B's reliability still outweighs C's adaptability concerns. But we need to move toward convergence. Since we have strong evidence for C now, I think shifting to C is reasonable.\n\nThus my public message: I agree with Agent 2, shift to C, explain why C's crew cooperation, decision quality, attention, stress resilience outweigh B's concerns. Mention B's lack of crew cooperation evidence and communication issues. Also note C's egocentric and not willing to further education as concerns but less critical.\n\nNow produce metadata JSON with vote Candidate C."}
